   "source": [
    "### 3.1. PubMedBert"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ce6b7392",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "PubMedBERT is a language model that was pretrained using millions of biomedical abstracts from the PubMed database. At this point, I would assume that this model will perform the best on my dataset, because it's already been pretrained on PubMed database. Let's see, if my guess is correct.\n",
    "\n",
    "Firstly, let's load the PubMedBERT model name and its corresponding tokenizer so the text can be converted into tokens that the model can understand."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 83,
   "id": "22d45d0f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "model_name = \"microsoft/BiomedNLP-PubMedBERT-base-uncased-abstract\"\n",
    "tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_name)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9ea8bdfa",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This function tokenizes each abstract into model-readable input and attaches the correct label."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 84,
   "id": "55514964",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "max_length = 512  \n",
    "\n",
    "def tokenize_with_labels(batch):\n",
    "    # tokenize text\n",
    "    enc = tokenizer(\n",
    "        batch[\"abstract\"],\n",
    "        padding=\"max_length\",\n",
    "        truncation=True,\n",
    "        max_length=max_length,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    # attach labels explicitly\n",
    "    enc[\"labels\"] = batch[\"label_id\"]\n",
    "    return enc\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a091f5d2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load cleaned CSVs\n",
    "train_df = pd.read_csv(\"pubmed_clean_train.csv\")\n",
    "val_df   = pd.read_csv(\"pubmed_clean_val.csv\")\n",
    "test_df  = pd.read_csv(\"pubmed_clean_test.csv\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Keep only necessary columns\n",
    "train_df = train_df[[\"abstract\", \"label_id\"]]\n",
    "val_df   = val_df[[\"abstract\", \"label_id\"]]\n",
    "test_df  = test_df[[\"abstract\", \"label_id\"]]\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "da6a8593",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "I already checked the data balance and I know that the data is imbalanced, so I decided on introducting the weights. The following code calculates balanced class weights based on the label distribution to help the model pay more attention to minority classes during training."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 86,
   "id": "343b90d3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Class weights: tensor([0.5011, 2.2150, 2.8214, 0.3548, 7.1818, 4.1579])\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "class_weights = compute_class_weight(\n",
    "    class_weight=\"balanced\",\n",
    "    classes=np.unique(train_df[\"label_id\"]),\n",
    "    y=train_df[\"label_id\"],\n",
    ")\n",
    "class_weights = torch.tensor(class_weights, dtype=torch.float)\n",
    "print(\"Class weights:\", class_weights)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 87,
   "id": "700f35e1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Convert to HuggingFace Datasets\n",
    "train_ds = Dataset.from_pandas(train_df)\n",
    "val_ds   = Dataset.from_pandas(val_df)\n",
    "test_ds  = Dataset.from_pandas(test_df)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ec3b2591",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Then I tokenize the dataset into model-ready tensors, removes unused text columns, and converts everything into PyTorch format so the model can train on it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a61dbbf0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
