    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6f617ac4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3.5. Decision Tree"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c45d60f8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "I have already fine-tuned 4 LLM models, but I out of curiosity I decided that it would be interesting also to compare the results with one of the Machine Learning models. The assumption wanted to make, to make a 'fair' comparison, was that I will not focus on additional features from the original dataset(so no extra feature engineering), I will just focus on abstract and my target variable. I also decided to fine-tune it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 173,
   "id": "66e327c2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "train_df = pd.read_csv(\"pubmed_clean_train.csv\")\n",
    "val_df   = pd.read_csv(\"pubmed_clean_val.csv\")\n",
    "test_df  = pd.read_csv(\"pubmed_clean_test.csv\")\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train, y_train = train_df[\"abstract\"].values, train_df[\"label_id\"].values\n",
    "X_val,   y_val   = val_df[\"abstract\"].values,   val_df[\"label_id\"].values\n",
    "X_test,  y_test  = test_df[\"abstract\"].values,  test_df[\"label_id\"].values"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 174,
   "id": "0fc29a07",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# recover label names (sorted by ID) for reports and plots\n",
    "all_df = pd.concat([train_df, val_df, test_df], axis=0)\n",
    "id2name = (\n",
    "    all_df[[\"label_id\", \"label_name\"]]\n",
    "    .drop_duplicates()\n",
    "    .sort_values(\"label_id\")\n",
    ")\n",
    "label_names = id2name[\"label_name\"].tolist()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "917bae30",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The Decision Tree algorithm does not have a built in vectorizer, which would transform the words into the numerical representation. That is why I need to aply the vecotrizier on my own - TF-IDF."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 175,
   "id": "e62be966",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "tfidf = TfidfVectorizer(\n",
    "    ngram_range=(1, 2),\n",
    "    min_df=3,\n",
    "    max_features=50_000\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7c763690",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The next piece of code converts the abstract text into TF-IDF numerical vectors, fitting the vocabulary only on the training set and applying the same transformation to validation and test sets."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 176,
   "id": "4fdb5138",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X_train_t = tfidf.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
    "X_val_t   = tfidf.transform(X_val)\n",
    "X_test_t  = tfidf.transform(X_test)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "723ecfe2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "In the next part, a Decision Tree model and a grid of possible hyperparameters are defined.\n",
    "Then, a 5-fold stratified cross-validation search is run to find which hyperparameter combination gives the best macro F1 score.\n",
    "Finally, the best-performing tree from the search is selected and used as the final classifier."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 177,
   "id": "4832af1e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Fitting 5 folds for each of 36 candidates, totalling 180 fits\n",
      "Best params from GridSearchCV: {'max_depth': None, 'min_samples_leaf': 2, 'min_samples_split': 5}\n",
      "Best CV macro F1: 0.5010376117213468\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "base_tree = DecisionTreeClassifier(\n",
    "    class_weight=\"balanced\",\n",
    "    random_state=42\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "param_grid = {\n",
    "    \"max_depth\": [10, 20, 30, None],\n",
    "    \"min_samples_split\": [2, 5, 10],\n",
    "    \"min_samples_leaf\": [1, 2, 5],\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "cv = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=42)\n",
    "\n",
    "grid = GridSearchCV(\n",
    "    estimator=base_tree,\n",
    "    param_grid=param_grid,\n",
    "    scoring=\"f1_macro\",\n",
    "    cv=cv,\n",
    "    n_jobs=-1,\n",
    "    verbose=1,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "grid.fit(X_train_t, y_train)\n",
    "\n",
